<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador trade surplus rose to $1.37 bln in 1996.</title>
<headline>Ecuador trade surplus rose to $1.37 bln in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador had a trade surplus of $1.37 billion in 1996, up from a $354 million surplus in 1995, the central bank said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Exports reached $4.86 billion, up from $4.41 billion in 1995. Imports fell to $3.48 billion from $4.06 billion.</p>
<p>In December 1996, Ecuador had a trade surplus of $166 million, up from $63 million in the same month of 1995.</p>
<p>((-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom 5932 258433))</p>
